WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.222
Coding Exercise 4 checks whether you understand the difference between matching and final filtering.

00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:13.052
The requirement says every patient must remain, while only Glucose lab rows should be allowed to match.

00:00:13.052 --> 00:00:16.497
The words every patient are the key to the problem.

00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:21.287
Complete the ON clause by adding the Glucose condition to the matching rule.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.062
Do not move that condition into WHERE.

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:28.722
If it goes into WHERE, patients without a Glucose match can disappear.

00:00:28.722 --> 00:00:31.577
Before running the query, predict the output.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:37.652
Every patient should appear. Some patients will have a Glucose test ID and result value.

00:00:37.652 --> 00:00:40.402
Other patients will have NULL lab fields.

00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:44.122
After Run and Check, inspect both types of rows.

00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:46.712
The goal is not only to pass the checker.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:51.422
The goal is to build the habit of deciding whether each condition belongs to matching or to final

00:00:51.422 --> 00:00:53.187
result filtering.
